# A paste into a terminal whose program is not reading its input — a
# build, `sleep`, `tail -f`, a server — is queued and the app stays
# responsive, as it is in ghostty or Terminal.app. The tty takes about a
# kilobyte and then stops; the rest waits in the session's outbox for
# the child to read it (`pty/outbox.zig`), never on the UI thread.
#
# 200 lines (4.6 KB, tabs included) pasted into `sleep 12`: right after
# the paste the child is still running, and the app still takes a
# command.
shell for i in $(seq 0 199); do printf 'line %04d\tcol\twith tab\n' $i; done > p.txt
open p.txt
command editor.use_vim
type "ggyG"
command view.toggle_tree
ex term sleep 12
wait 500
expect screen contains "sleep 12"
command term.paste
wait 200
expect screen lacks "[exited"
ex rename still-here
expect screen contains "still-here"
